    "body": "## Context\n\nPR #67 added `checkAgeReviewDeadlines()` which handles:\n- Slack alerts for cases approaching deadline (within 2 days, 12h dedupe)\n- Auto-close of expired cases (state → `denied_closed`)\n\nThe function exists but is never called from the worker's `scheduled` handler in `worker/src/index.ts`.\n\n## What to do\n\nAdd one call in the `scheduled` method (after the pre-auth nonce cleanup):\n\n```typescript\n// Age review deadline checks\ntry {\n  await checkAgeReviewDeadlines(env);\n} catch (error) {\n  console.error('[scheduled] Failed to check age review deadlines:', error);\n}\n```\n\n## Prerequisites\n\nWire this up once:\n- `SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL` secret is set on staging/prod\n- Cases are actually being created (mobile reports or moderator tooling)\n- Keycast enforcement (Track C) is in place so auto-close has real consequences\n\n## Related\n\n- PR #67 — age review clock (defines the function)\n- Track C (Keycast suspension) — without enforcement, auto-close is cosmetic",
